>   My basic suggestion is that the game could would benefit form the
> removal of randomly generated w.o.p.s and  some compensatory additions.
 
> 1. w.o.p. on castle level.
> How about replacing the wand of wishing on the castle level with a wand
> of polymorph?

Eeek, no, the castle level is fine, I want that wand of wishing. It's a
good idea that a powerful wand is given as a reward for a difficult task,
and perhaps that idea could be extended in a different direction.

Proposal: Medusa should carry a wand of polymorph.

 - Defeat of a very dangerous monster should bring great rewards,
   i.e. dead dragons and dead cockatrices are useful. So far my
   only reward for killing Medusa has been a pile of rocks.

 - Because there's only one Medusa, poly-abuses would be kept down.

 - Each Minotaur already carries a wand of digging, which presumably
   is how he carved out that maze.

 - Medusa transforms her victims: how?

 - Perhaps it was by careless use of a wand of polymorph that
   Medusa got that unbelievably ugly face!
 
